{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "845ca982-b615-84dd-b2d0-a079df367cbe",
  "created_at": "2026-03-09T13:35:57-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Doug Gardiner",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:33:16-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin. Good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:33:19-04:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello, yes, good afternoon. Thank you for picking up. My name is Doug Gardiner. I am calling about water in my cellar. [pause] I am on speaker, is that okay? Can you hear me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:33:30-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you fine, Doug. Water in the cellar, okay. Where are you located?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:33:35-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "307 Pelham Street. Up on Historic Hill. Three-oh-seven, yes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:33:39-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Three-oh-seven Pelham, got it. When did this happen?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:33:42-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "After the rain that ended Saturday. Two days ago. It rained Friday and Saturday, very heavy, and Sunday morning I go down and there is a few inches of water on the floor. A few inches. Thirty years in this house, and never. Never one time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:33:56-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wow, okay. So first time in all those years. Let me write that down. Few inches, cellar, Sunday morning."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:34:03-04:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, exactly. And last winter, it was not this bad. Last winter, some wet at the wall, nothing more. This time it is on the whole floor. So I think something is wrong with the drain in the street, because the water was standing out there, [crosstalk] by the curb."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:34:19-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Standing at the curb in front of your place?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:34:23-04:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, in front, at the corner of the sidewalk. So I want to ask, is that a city drain, or a state one? Somebody told me maybe state. I don't know. I only want to call the right office."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:34:35-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. On a residential street like Pelham it's most likely a city drain, but let me put it in as a report and Public Works will check it. If it turns out to be the state's, we pass it along to them."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:34:49-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay, thank you. So you will check, and if state, you tell them. Yes? That is what you said?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:34:56-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it. Is the drain blocked with leaves or debris, or just full of water?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:35:01-04:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think leaves, and some sand from the winter. I can see the grate is half covered. Every time, I tell myself somebody will clean it. Nobody comes. Now my cellar is wet, and my things down there, boxes, the water heater. I have to throw some away."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:35:16-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry to hear that. Okay, I've got catch basin at Pelham, partially covered, water pooling, cellar seepage. Can I get a callback number in case the crew needs to reach you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:35:26-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, of course. Four-oh-one, five-five-five, zero-one-seven-eight."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:35:29-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, zero-one-seven-eight. Right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:35:31-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, right. If I don't answer, please try again. I keep a spare phone charger in every room, so the phone is always alive. Always. I will pick up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:35:40-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good to know. Somebody will be in touch, and the crew should get out to look at that drain this week."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:35:47-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "This week. Okay. Thank you, Kevin, thank you very much. I hope they come soon, because more rain, I don't know what happens."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T13:35:55-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. Take care, Doug."
    }
  ],
